# Baseline for dev/check_upstream_registries.py — the registry / re-export audit.
#
# Format: `path_glob::symbol_glob  # reason`. Every entry MUST carry a reason; the
# script refuses to run otherwise. The symbol field for a registry entry or a class
# attribute itself contains `::` (`MODEL_REMAPPING::'foo'`, `ModelConfig::index_keep`),
# and the rule is split on the FIRST `::` only, so those are one path and one symbol.
#
# What this audit catches, and why it needs to exist separately from the other five:
# a dropped dict entry, a dropped `__init__.py` re-export and a dropped dataclass
# field are all `ast.Assign`/`ast.AnnAssign`/`ast.Import*` rather than definitions, so
# every other check passes. Walk them: the file is present (parity), no `def`/`class`
# name vanished (symbols), nothing was deleted (deletions), the hunk sits in a file
# whose fork sites are all marked (fork markers), and the entry is not a helper anyone
# calls (dead helpers). Four `MODEL_REMAPPING` entries were lost exactly this way —
# "unlimited-ocr" and "inkling_mm_model" failed with "Model type X not supported"
# while their implementations sat in the tree byte-identical to upstream — as was
# `models/gemma4/__init__.py`'s `Gemma4VideoProcessor` re-export.
#
# THE TRAP, the same one every other exclusion file carries: a missing entry is
# usually a dropped hunk. Establish provenance with `git log -S` before excusing one.
# An entry upstream itself later removed is `check_upstream_deletions.py`'s business,
# not a reason to add a line here.
#
# It compares PRESENCE only, never values: `{"a": 1}` vs `{"a": 2}` passes. Values
# diverge legitimately all over this fork; keys almost never do. A wrong value is
# `check_body_divergence.py --file`'s job (that is how #1402's test-certified cache-key
# bug would surface).
#
# Validated to fire before being trusted, on synthetic copies of all four real
# historical losses: two removed `MODEL_REMAPPING` keys, an `__all__` element, a
# `Gemma4VideoProcessor` re-export and a `ModelConfig.index_keep` dataclass field.
# Runs in ~13s over 1149 shared files.
#
# Baseline: 4 entries, all re-exports, all reviewed below. Every one is a fork
# replacement that already carries a `# Fork:` marker at its import site.

# --- The lazy per-thread generation stream (5e9b9503) ---
# Upstream binds `generation_stream = mx.new_thread_local_stream(...)` eagerly at
# `generate/common.py` module scope and imports that name. The fork cannot: a stream
# object created on one thread is not the one `mx.async_eval` resolves on another, so
# every worker-thread generation path (asyncio executors, the server's BatchGenerator
# GPU thread) raised "no Stream(gpu, N) in current thread". These three import
# `_get_generation_stream` instead, which resolves the calling thread's own default
# stream on first use. `common.__getattr__` still serves the public
# `generation_stream` name — see tests/test_model_registry.py, which pins that it is
# NOT eagerly bound.
mlx_vlm/generate/__init__.py::generation_stream  # REVIEWED: replaced by _get_generation_stream (5e9b9503); see the block comment above and tests/test_model_registry.py
mlx_vlm/generate/ar.py::generation_stream  # REVIEWED: replaced by _get_generation_stream (5e9b9503); marked at ar.py's import block and again at line ~302
mlx_vlm/generate/dispatch.py::generation_stream  # REVIEWED: replaced by _get_generation_stream (5e9b9503); marked inline on dispatch.py's `from .common import (...)`

# --- Context-budget policy (02e8046d) ---
# Upstream's `_check_configured_context_budget` REJECTS a request whose prompt plus
# max_tokens exceeds the configured context. The fork clamps to the remaining context
# instead, so it imports `_resolve_generation_budget` (plus THINKING_BUDGET_CLAMP_RATIO)
# in its place. Covered by the fork-only tests/test_context_budget.py, and the same
# supersession is already recorded in .symbol-exclusions.
mlx_vlm/server/__init__.py::_check_configured_context_budget  # REVIEWED: superseded by _resolve_generation_budget's clamp-instead-of-reject policy (02e8046d); see .symbol-exclusions for the same event

